in  space and my dream was shattered  only later in life i learned that there  are actually  many ways to listen and that thinking  through sound in space  might actually mean to consider an  extended form of listening  which can be done through different  antennas or by extending the range of  messengers one listens to  maybe for instance cosmic rays different  types of particles  or waves that  maybe to a scientist space could  actually be full of sounds  during my collide at cern and barcelona  residency  i told a physicist about my  re-evaluation or expanded understanding  of perception  he responded to me with this story every  time  i watched the stars with my young  daughter i tried to tell her i tried to  explain  that what she is really looking at is  the neverending resonance of the big  bang  the light of the stars we see today is  also the momentary state of resonance  of the loudest sound the universe has  ever heard  my conclusion is that standard  resolutions can be useful determinations  they can work to make our everyday life  run smooth they make  things function but they're also  presumptions which puts them by default  at  risk to preclude alternatives to  perpetuate harmful clutched ways of  running  listening or understanding and finally  they can block experiments  in new ways or other ways of seeing  impossible images and the latent image  space  during my time at cern i interviewed  over 40 scientists  i asked them imagine you could obtain an  impossible image  of any object or phenomenon that you  think is important  with no limits on spatial temporal  energy  signal to noise or cost resolutions  what image would you create  the collection of impossible images i  have collected so far is fantastic  they already illustrate a diverse array  of limits on resolution or impossibility  but also on the technologies of what  imaging can be  itself a preliminary categorization of  impossible images  would entail images that are impossible  due to spatial or time or other types of  resolution  images that were deemed impossible in  the past but that have become  possible today images that were possible  in the past  but that are no longer possible images  depending on speculation  disbelief or imagination and images of  objects that can only be  inferred involving a substantial  signal-to-noise bounty  i organized a collection of impossible  images in a low poly rendition of what i  called  unquantifiable blob of impossible images  the blob or binary large object  is home to the collection of impossible  images that all together  illustrate the concept of impossible  image and its relationships  with affordance resolutions and  compromises  when you enter the 3d space in front of  the blob  the visitor is welcomed by the angel of  history she stands there pointing to the  blob  a map reminiscing the realms of  compression complexities  standing right beside her while behind  her a staircase to nowhere points  upwards  one enters the blob through a portal  imaging the shadow of dark matter  on the right an image of the inside of a  proton shows  three quarks the tiniest known building  blocks of the universe  they are smaller than a wavelength of  light  in front of us an image of the quantum  vacuum  at a slice of plank constant time ish  shattering  space  left of it a missing image  and beside it an image of a sunset  on the labrador coast from susan  shupley's film candeson lie  in which shupley describes the story of  a photographic image that denied to  abide  the rules of the optical regime  normally these images would have never  found their way to our eyes  but the hypothetical realms of the blob  offer pasture  to these impossible renders  they show that thinking through  impossibilities means thinking through  liminalities it means to consider and  possibly expand the limits  of understanding what is possible  the blob gives a shape to the latent  image space  the space of any and all images past and  future  which in reality has become a fragmented  space of stacked predetermined actions  and affordances  consolidated in resolutions  standing here different axes of  affordance  titled x y z and alpha cut the blob  they define what is possible to resolve  but also  what images are compromised or in other  words  will never be rendered  through my research into resolutions and  impossible image  i see a need to keep fragmenting the  stacks  of the computational image but i also  recognize a growing ecology of theories  around the liminal image space including  but not limited to  virilio's synthetic image pharaoh keys  operational images rubenstein's  fragmented photographic images  tagline's invisible images dances  discorrelated images  fluecer's techno images for burdens  computational images  and of course styles poor image  in a time of exploded and exponent  photography  a time that recognizes that photography  no longer needs to be representational  lens or light based these theories help  us to understand not only what the image  is built off  but also what an image is or what the  latent image space  can be  the latent image can be used as a tool  to expand our perception and in doing so  it can open new ways  to see  you


